**Uyghurs**

The Kingdom of Qocho (also known as the Idiqut state) was established by the Uyghurs in the 9th century after the collapse of the Uyghur Khaganate. Its rulers seasonally relocated between the summer capital at Beiting (Peiting) in the Tian Shan mountains and the winter capital at Qocho (Gaochang) in the Turpan Depression. This practice reflected their semi-nomadic heritage adapted to the region's climate.

\boxed{Uyghurs}

